# Isolated controls: amendment tests must assert durable state, not response wording
#
# Requirement under test (verification contract): "explicitly confirmed
# semantically identical rehydration succeeds, while real target/revision/
# contract/task/status/session/ownership changes reject stale consent without
# mutation or an audit claim" — and isolated controls must demonstrate
# detection of the MEANINGFUL regressions "without relying on incidental
# object identity, wording or test totals".
#
# The previous tests asserted three response strings:
#   /target changed during scope confirmation/i
#   /not confirmed/i
#   /AUDIT PENDING/
# Those pin human-facing English, so a diagnostic-only rewording failed the
# suite while the protected behavior was intact. They were replaced with
# durable assertions: persisted goal revision, deep-equal unchanged goal and
# no stored pendingCompletion on rejection, and a stored pendingCompletion
# attemptId on success.
#
# Control surface: disposable copy /tmp/glla-w1 (since removed), carrying
# extensions/, scripts/, tests/, package.json, tsconfig.json, a symlinked
# node_modules, and bunfig.toml.
#
# SETUP CORRECTION (recorded because it initially produced a FALSE failure):
# the first copy omitted bunfig.toml, whose [test] preload
# (./tests/harness/setup.ts) provides the hermetic global-settings redirect.
# Without it the UNMODIFIED copy failed 2/14 on
# "ctx.modelRegistry.find" inside resolveAuditorModel — an environment defect
# of the control, not a product or test finding. After adding bunfig.toml the
# unmodified copy passed 14/14, which is the required baseline before a
# control proves anything.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BASELINE (unmodified copy, bunfig.toml present):
#    14 pass
#     0 fail
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROL 1 — diagnostic-only rewording must PASS (behavior untouched).
# Rewrote all three messages in extensions/loops/goal-tools.ts:
#   "The target changed during scope confirmation; ..."
#     -> "Consent no longer matches the current goal target, so nothing was
#         amended or claimed."
#   "Scope amendment not confirmed. ..."
#     -> "Amendment declined. Objective, contract and completion claim are all
#         unchanged."
#   "AUDIT PENDING — nonterminal. ..."
#     -> "Detached audit queued — not yet terminal. Claim persisted; compaction
#         check happens at the next owned idle boundary. Stop here."
#
#    14 pass
#     0 fail
#   control-1-exit=0
#
# RESULT: correctly PASSES. The suite no longer depends on response wording;
# an agent may reword a diagnostic explanation without failing the gate. Under
# the previous wording assertions this same edit failed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROL 2 — the real regression must FAIL on the DURABLE assertion.
# Restored the ORIGINAL object-identity fence in place of the semantic-authority
# fence:
#   if (auditGeneration !== sessionGeneration || state.goal !== amendmentGoal)
# Rehydration still satisfies every semantic check but replaces the JS object,
# so this is the exact false rejection the objective asks to repair.
#
#   44 |  assert.equal(durable?.revision, 2, "the confirmed amendment advanced
#       |                              ^ the audited revision on disk");
#   AssertionError: the confirmed amendment advanced the audited revision on disk
#   (fail) confirmed amendment survives identical rehydration (task key reorder=false)
#   (fail) confirmed amendment survives identical rehydration (task key reorder=true)
#   ...
#   control-2-exit=1
#
# RESULT: correctly FAILS, and it fails on the DURABLE revision assertion
# (test line 44), not on message text — proving the replacement assertions
# still detect the meaningful regression the contract protects.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live repository source (unmodified): tests/amendment-confirmation-fence.test.ts
# runs 14 passed / 0 failed, and a grep for the three former wording patterns
# in that file returns no matches.
